# Trove Web ↔ Mobile parity

This repo is the **browser companion** to **Trove Mobile** (`../trove` or the **Trove Mobile** root in `trove.code-workspace`).

## Source of truth

| Concern | Mobile (wins) | Web (follows) |
|---------|---------------|---------------|
| Save types, schema | `trove/types/index.ts` | `trove-web/lib/types.ts` |
| Library filters, chips | `trove/lib/libraryFilterChips.ts` | `trove-web/lib/libraryFilterChips.ts` |
| Save card layout | `trove/components/SaveCard.tsx` | `trove-web/components/SaveCard.tsx` |
| Checklist UI | `trove/components/NoteBodyEditor.tsx` | Never show raw `- [ ]` on web |
| Design tokens | `trove/constants/theme.ts` | `trove-web/lib/theme.ts` + `--trove-*` |
| Supabase project | `trove/.env.local` | Same URL + anon key (`scripts/sync-web-env.ps1`) |

When mobile and web disagree on Library / Collections / save detail UX, **update web, not mobile** (see `trove/AGENTS.md` § Trove Web).

## Icons

Do not recreate App Store / Google Play badges or other trademark logos. Use
`react-icons/si` via `components/StoreBadgeLinks.tsx`. No emoji as product icons.

## Before porting a feature

1. Read the mobile screen (`trove/app/…`) and its `lib/` helpers.
2. Port **pure** logic first (no React Native imports); add `node:test` in `trove-web/lib/`.
3. Match existing web chrome (`AppShell`, `FilterBar`, `SaveCard`, tokens) — no one-off layouts.

## Graphify

Mobile repo has `graphify-out/` — run `graphify query` from **Trove Mobile** root before cross-file exploration. Web repo has no graph yet; use mobile graph for architecture questions.

## Dev commands

```powershell
# Mobile (device / Expo)
cd trove
npx expo start --web   # layout preview only in VM

# Web
cd trove-web
npm run dev            # http://localhost:3000

# Shared Supabase keys (from mobile .env.local)
cd trove
.\scripts\sync-web-env.ps1
```
